    "fallout-ssl": {
        "reason": "Decided never-fixes, all inside #define bodies, in three shapes. (1) Body left empty for the modder to fill: `#define FFIELD_PID ()` (genffld, sprtrp0). These are templates - the error exists only while the placeholder is unfilled, and filling it in makes the file parse with no grammar change, so flagging them is correct signal rather than a gap. (2) Body that is a syntactic fragment completed at the expansion site - ends on a bare `if (cond)` with no `then` (hcdoc, vcdrtroy). (3) Source the compiler never sees, inside macros that are never expanded: one unbalanced closing paren (ncftully) and a doubled line continuation (ncnikki). Not counted toward the allowlist-shrink metric. The unterminated-final-statement gap that covered 13 other files is fixed - see macro_body/_macro_tail in the grammar.",
