    "weidu-d": {
        "reason": "Decided never-fix: a bare %var% standing in a say-text slot (`CHAIN ... %kivan17%`, which OUTER_SPRINT sets to the strref `#32793`). The grammar's _text accepts string/@N/#strref/(AT \"..\") and deliberately not a variable, even though the neighbouring transition slot has macro_expansion. Not counted toward the allowlist-shrink metric.",
        "files": ["BG1NPC/bg1npc/phase2/dlg/x#kivantazok_ee.d"]
    },
    "weidu-tp2": {
        "reason": "Decided never-fix: this file closes one more END than it opens (8 BEGIN, 9 END). WeiDU tolerates the stray END - verified by INCLUDEing the file from a wrapper tp2, which installs clean, and reduced to `ACTION_IF 1 THEN BEGIN ... END END`, which parses too. Matching that would mean accepting unbalanced BEGIN/END everywhere, losing a real error signal on every genuinely unbalanced file, so the grammar stays stricter than WeiDU here. Not counted toward the allowlist-shrink metric. The other tp2 entry, nested block comments, is fixed - the grammar now scans them externally.",
        "files": ["BG1NPC/bg1npc/core/tpa/a64_beregost.tpa"]
    },
    "weidu-tra": {
        "reason": "worldmap.tra files use non-numeric `@BGT_781001` keys, which are not standard WeiDU tra - the tra lexer (WeiDUorg/weidu src/tlexer.in) only accepts `@['-']?['0'-'9']+`. These are preprocessed by BGT, not parsed directly; a grammar fix is not appropriate. The charset, two-sound, and percent-string gaps that previously errored here are now fixed.",
